STATE,COMPOMENTS AND RE-RENDERING

whatever is used with use- is a hook in reactt

State is data stored inside a component that can change over time.

count     → current state value
setCount  → function to update count
0         → initial value

State = changing data that React keeps track of for a component.

Props are data passed from a parent component to a child component.
Props = information a parent gives to a child

-rendering means React runs a component again to determine what its UI should look like now.

State changed
     ↓
App runs again
     ↓
count = 1
     ↓
React sees the new UI
     ↓
Browser displays 1

| State                            | Props                                      |
| -------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------ |
| Data managed by a component      | Data passed to a component                 |
| Can change using setter          | Child should treat props as read-only      |
| `useState()` commonly creates it | Passed through JSX                         |
| Causes updates when changed      | Changed props can cause child to re-render |
| `count`                          | `props.count`                              |


Remember this one sentence
State is changing data → props pass data between components → when relevant state/props change, React re-renders the component to update the UI.

